# Global saved skills

When a user adds a **custom skill** (via "Other — type your own") anywhere in Ledger, it must be remembered **for that user** on every form that selects skills.

## Storage

- Server: `user_preferences.saved_skills` via `GET/PUT /api/preferences` (`static/ledger_prefs.js`)
- Client cache / offline fallback: `localStorage` key `ledger_saved_skills`
- Stored as an array of `{ module, skill }` objects
- On first load, empty server prefs import from localStorage once, then sync both ways
- All skill pickers must use `templates/macros/skills.html` + `LedgerPrefs`

## Behavior

- Custom skills are saved automatically when used — no opt-in checkbox
- Built-in module skills are never duplicated into saved storage
- Saved skills appear in a **Saved** optgroup for the matching module on every picker (daily goal, skill used)
- Pickers listen for `ledger-saved-skills-changed` and `storage` events to stay in sync

## When adding skill UI

- Reuse `templates/macros/skills.html` and `static/ledger_prefs.js`
- Do not introduce alternate keys or browser-only custom skill lists for picker UI
